{
  "questions": [
    {
      "area": "Users",
      "question": "Who is the target team and how big are they?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "Small startup teams (5–25 people), single workspace per team", "tradeoff": "Simple data model, easy to ship, but limits enterprise upside"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Mid-size orgs (25–200) with multiple sub-teams under one workspace", "tradeoff": "Adds team/group hierarchy and permissions complexity"},
        {"label": "C", "description": "Anyone — solo to enterprise", "tradeoff": "Forces generic UX and delays product-market fit"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — keep v1 focused on small startup teams to ship fast and validate the Slack-native loop"
    },
    {
      "area": "Auth / Tenancy",
      "question": "How do users sign in and how is tenancy modeled?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "Sign in with Slack (OAuth); workspace = tenant", "tradeoff": "Tightest fit with Slack notifications; no Slack means no app"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Email/password + invite links, Slack connected separately", "tradeoff": "More flexible but adds an account system to maintain"},
        {"label": "C", "description": "Google SSO + Slack connection", "tradeoff": "Familiar to teams but two integrations to wire up"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — Slack OAuth as the only auth path keeps the product cohesive and removes a screen"
    },
    {
      "area": "Core loop",
      "question": "What is the primary surface for creating and completing todos?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "Web app primary, Slack used for notifications + slash command to add", "tradeoff": "Familiar UX, but two surfaces to maintain"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Slack-first: everything via slash commands and message actions, web is read-only dashboard", "tradeoff": "Lowest friction but constrained UI for editing"},
        {"label": "C", "description": "Web only; Slack is notifications outbound only", "tradeoff": "Simplest build but ignores Slack as an input channel"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — web app for editing/triage, Slack for quick-add and notifications"
    },
    {
      "area": "Data model — tags",
      "question": "Are tags free-form or workspace-defined?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "Free-form strings, autocomplete from existing tags in the workspace", "tradeoff": "Easy to use, can fragment over time"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Admin-defined tag list only", "tradeoff": "Cleaner taxonomy, but adds admin overhead"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — free-form with autocomplete; defer governance to a later version"
    },
    {
      "area": "Data model — assignment",
      "question": "Can a todo be assigned, and to how many people?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "Single assignee + creator", "tradeoff": "Clear ownership, simple model"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Multiple assignees", "tradeoff": "Flexible but ownership becomes ambiguous"},
        {"label": "C", "description": "No assignment, just shared list", "tradeoff": "Simplest but undermines team value"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — single assignee + creator is the standard team-todo pattern"
    },
    {
      "area": "Slack notifications — triggers",
      "question": "What events trigger Slack notifications?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "Assignment, due-date reminders (1 day before + day of), and @mentions in todo comments", "tradeoff": "Useful set without being noisy"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Every change (create, edit, complete, comment)", "tradeoff": "High signal loss from noise"},
        {"label": "C", "description": "Only due-date reminders", "tradeoff": "Minimal value, misses assignment moment"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — assignment + due reminders + mentions covers the high-value moments"
    },
    {
      "area": "Slack notifications — delivery",
      "question": "Where do notifications land in Slack?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "DM to the assignee from the app", "tradeoff": "Private and direct, doesn't clutter channels"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Configurable channel per workspace", "tradeoff": "Team visibility but noisy and impersonal"},
        {"label": "C", "description": "Both: DM the assignee, optional channel digest", "tradeoff": "Best coverage but more config surface"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — DM only in v1, with action buttons (Complete / Snooze) on the message"
    },
    {
      "area": "Permissions",
      "question": "Who can edit or delete a todo?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "Any workspace member can edit any todo; only creator or assignee can delete", "tradeoff": "Open and collaborative, low friction"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Only creator/assignee can edit; admins can delete anything", "tradeoff": "Stricter, fewer accidents, more friction"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — small teams need low friction; deletion is the only guarded action"
    },
    {
      "area": "Scale",
      "question": "What scale should v1 target?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "Up to 500 workspaces, 25 users each, 10k todos per workspace", "tradeoff": "Comfortable for a single Postgres instance"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Plan for 10k+ workspaces from day one", "tradeoff": "Premature optimization for an unvalidated product"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — size for early adopters; revisit when traction warrants"
    },
    {
      "area": "Out of scope",
      "question": "What should v1 explicitly exclude?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "Exclude: subtasks, recurring todos, file attachments, custom fields, mobile apps, calendar sync, billing/paid tiers", "tradeoff": "Keeps v1 shippable in weeks"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Include recurring todos and subtasks in v1", "tradeoff": "Doubles the data model and UI work"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — defer everything beyond the stated core (tags, due dates, Slack)"
    },
    {
      "area": "Success definition",
      "question": "How is v1 success measured?",
      "options": [
        {"label": "A", "description": "20 active workspaces with ≥3 active users completing ≥10 todos/week, 4 weeks post-launch", "tradeoff": "Concrete, measurable, modest"},
        {"label": "B", "description": "Vague: 'people are using it'", "tradeoff": "Untestable"}
      ],
      "recommendation": "Option A — concrete usage thresholds drive product decisions"
    }
  ],
  "recommendations": [
    {"area": "Users", "recommendation": "Target small startup teams (5–25 people), one workspace per team", "rationale": "Smallest viable audience that exercises the team + Slack value prop"},
    {"area": "Auth", "recommendation": "Slack OAuth only; Slack workspace = app tenant", "rationale": "Slack is required for the headline feature, so make it the only sign-in path"},
    {"area": "Core loop", "recommendation": "Web app primary for triage and editing; Slack slash command (/todo) for quick-add and message actions", "rationale": "Web UI handles the editing surface, Slack handles capture and follow-through"},
    {"area": "Tags", "recommendation": "Free-form tag strings with autocomplete from existing workspace tags", "rationale": "Low friction, common pattern, no admin overhead"},
    {"area": "Assignment", "recommendation": "One assignee per todo, plus creator tracked separately", "rationale": "Clear ownership; matches Slack DM model"},
    {"area": "Slack notifications", "recommendation": "DM the assignee on assignment, on @mention in comments, and at T-24h and T-0 for due dates; messages include Complete and Snooze buttons", "rationale": "High-signal moments only; actionable from inside Slack"},
    {"area": "Permissions", "recommendation": "Any workspace member can create/edit any todo; only creator or assignee can delete", "rationale": "Optimizes for collaboration in small teams while protecting against accidental loss"},
    {"area": "Scale", "recommendation": "Design for 500 workspaces × 25 users × 10k todos each", "rationale": "Realistic early-adopter scale; single Postgres is sufficient"},
    {"area": "Out of scope", "recommendation": "No subtasks, recurring todos, attachments, custom fields, mobile apps, calendar sync, or billing in v1", "rationale": "Keeps the build focused on the three named features"},
    {"area": "Success", "recommendation": "20 active workspaces with ≥3 active users each completing ≥10 todos/week by week 4 post-launch", "rationale": "Measurable target tied to actual team usage"}
  ],
  "rewritten_braindump": "# Team Todo App with Slack Notifications\n\n## Core Product\n\nA web-based todo application for small startup teams (5–25 people) that integrates natively with Slack. Each Slack workspace becomes a tenant. Users sign in with Slack OAuth. Todos have a title, optional description, optional due date, free-form tags, a single assignee, and a creator. The web app is the primary surface for browsing, filtering, and editing; Slack is the surface for quick capture (slash command) and notifications (DMs with action buttons).\n\n## Users\n\n- Small startup teams, 5–25 members per Slack workspace.\n- Mixed technical levels; users are already comfortable with Slack.\n- One Slack workspace = one app workspace = one tenant.\n\n## Auth\n\n- Sign in with Slack OAuth only. No email/password, no other SSO.\n- A user's identity is their Slack user within a workspace.\n- Workspace install is performed once by any member; subsequent members sign in via Slack OAuth and are auto-provisioned.\n\n## Core Loop\n\nIn a single session, a user:\n1. Opens the web app (or `/todo` in Slack) and creates a todo with title, optional due date, optional tags, and an assignee.\n2. The assignee receives a Slack DM from the app with the todo details and Complete / Snooze buttons.\n3. The assignee either completes from Slack (button) or opens the web app to edit, comment, or reassign.\n4. As due dates approach, the assignee receives reminder DMs at T-24h and T-0.\n5. Comments with @mentions DM the mentioned user.\n\n## Data Model (entities)\n\n- **Workspace** — one per Slack workspace; holds install token and settings.\n- **User** — Slack user identity scoped to a workspace.\n- **Todo** — title, description, due_at (nullable), status (open/completed), creator_id, assignee_id (nullable), workspace_id, created_at, completed_at.\n- **Tag** — free-form string scoped to a workspace; many-to-many with Todo via TodoTag.\n- **Comment** — text on a todo, with author_id and created_at.\n\n## Features (v1)\n\n- Create, edit, complete, delete, and reassign todos.\n- Free-form tags with autocomplete from existing workspace tags.\n- Due dates with calendar picker.\n- Filter and search todos by assignee, tag, due date range, and status.\n- Slack slash command `/todo <title>` to quick-add a todo (assigns to invoker by default).\n- Slack DM notifications on: assignment, @mention in a comment, T-24h before due, T-0 at due time.\n- DM messages include Complete and Snooze (1d, 3d, 1w) buttons.\n- Per-user Slack notification preferences (toggle each trigger type on/off).\n\n## Permissions\n\n- Any workspace member can create, edit, comment on, complete, or reassign any todo.\n- Only the creator or current assignee can delete a todo.\n- No admin role in v1.\n\n## Scale Targets\n\n- Up to 500 workspaces.\n- Up to 25 users per workspace.\n- Up to 10,000 todos per workspace.\n- Single Postgres instance is sufficient.\n\n## Integrations\n\n- Slack: OAuth, slash commands, interactive message buttons, chat.postMessage for DMs, Events API for handling button actions.\n- No other third-party integrations in v1.\n\n## Out of Scope (v1)\n\n- Subtasks and dependencies.\n- Recurring todos.\n- File attachments.\n- Custom fields.\n- Mobile apps (web is responsive but not native).\n- Calendar sync (Google/Outlook).\n- Email notifications.\n- Billing, paid tiers, usage limits.\n- Multi-workspace switching for a single user.\n- Public sharing or external collaborators.\n- Admin role and audit logs.\n\n## Success Definition\n\nFour weeks after launch:\n- 20 active workspaces.\n- Each active workspace has ≥3 active users.\n- Each active workspace completes ≥10 todos per week.\n- ≥50% of completions originate from a Slack action button (validates Slack-native loop).\n",
  "suggested_action": "run spec-pipeline"
}
